# Env is the door for a SCRIPT to lay files beside its protocol.
# It computes NOTHING. The run folder belongs to the vessel, which fixes
# cRunFolder once per run in $runExecutor; this class only asks for it.
# One source for the path. Cookbook D6c.
# A $construct cannot abort the method that entered, so a failure is
# CARRIED in $ok and $why instead of raised. A script that writes must
# ask $ok, or it will believe an empty path.
# env_class v1 (2026-08-29).
Calculate iOk as kFalse
Calculate iWhy as ''
Calculate iPath as ''
Calculate count as $clib.$classes.ExecutorConsole.$insts().$count
If count=1
	Set reference ref to $clib.$classes.ExecutorConsole.$insts().$first()
	Calculate iPath as ref.$runFolder()
	If len(iPath)
		Calculate iOk as kTrue
	Else
		Calculate iWhy as 'the console has no run folder for this run yet'
	End If
Else
	Calculate iWhy as con(count,' console instances are open, so this run cannot be attributed to one')
End If